# Cursor Rules for CRX Manager V1.0

## Project
Agricultural product distribution management system for Crop RX Solutions.
React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind CSS + Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage, Realtime).
Deployed to Vercel. Tests with Playwright.

## User Context
The project owner is a beginner with zero coding experience. Explain changes simply. Do not assume prior knowledge.

## Stack Rules
- Use React 18 with TypeScript (strict mode)
- Use Tailwind CSS for all styling. Brand color: `crx-green` (#28A26A)
- Use Lucide React for all icons. Do not install other icon or UI libraries
- Use Supabase client from `src/lib/db.ts` (singleton). Never create additional Supabase clients
- All shared TypeScript types live in `src/types/index.ts`
- All pages are lazy-loaded via `React.lazy()` in `src/App.tsx`

## Database Rules
- All schema changes MUST go through migration files in `supabase/migrations/`
- RLS (Row Level Security) is enabled on ALL 25 tables -- never disable it
- After every `.update()` or `.delete()`, call `checkMutationResult()` from `src/lib/db.ts`
- Three user roles: admin, sales_rep, driver. RLS helpers: `is_admin()`, `is_sales_rep()`, `is_driver()`

## Code Patterns
- Log important actions with `logActivity()` from `src/lib/activityLogger.ts`
- Use `generateIdempotencyKey()` from `src/lib/idempotency.ts` for critical writes
- Compress images before upload with `compressImage()` from `src/lib/imageCompression.ts`
- Check online status with `useOnlineStatus()` hook for offline-capable features

## File Structure
- Pages: `src/pages/` (one file per route)
- Components: `src/components/` (grouped by feature)
- Utilities: `src/lib/` (database, PDF, CSV, OCR, offline, etc.)
- Hooks: `src/hooks/`
- Types: `src/types/index.ts`
- Migrations: `supabase/migrations/`
- Tests: `tests/e2e/`

## Environment
- Env vars: `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (must have VITE_ prefix)
- Dev server: `npm run dev` (port 5173)
- Build: `npm run build`
- Tests: `npm run test:e2e`

## Key Documentation
- `CONTEXT.md` -- Full business context, data model, all 25 tables
- `DATABASE_RELATIONSHIPS.md` -- Entity relationships
- `SCHEMA_QUICK_REFERENCE.sql` -- Complete SQL schema
- `TESTING.md` -- Testing guide
- `DEPLOYMENT.md` -- Deployment guide

